14. ERROR HANDLING

Define a small, consistent error approach: typed error codes on the server, a mapping to friendly messages on the client, full detail only in server logs. Never show raw stack traces or backend internals to citizens.

Cover and test each case:

Scenario	Expected behaviour
Google Sign-In cancelled / popup blocked / failed	Friendly message, can retry
Email registration failure (exists, weak password, network)	Specific inline message
Login failure	Neutral, clear message; no account enumeration
Password reset failure	Clear message; neutral wording
Image upload failure	Input preserved, retry offered
Firestore write failure	No false success; input preserved
